      <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #ffffff; line-height: 1.6; margin: 0;">
        Medicare Extra Help (Low Income Subsidy) is a federal program that pays your Part D drug plan monthly premium, eliminates your deductible, and caps prescription copays at <strong style="color: #C9933A;">$4.90 for generics and $12.15 for brand names in 2026</strong>. Single income limit: $1,985/mo ($17,220 assets). Married limit: $2,685/mo ($34,360 assets). Primary home and 1 car are excluded.
      </p>
    </div>

    <!-- Problem Statement -->
    <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #4B5A6E; line-height: 1.6; margin: 1rem 0;">
