  <section style="margin-block: var(--space-10);" aria-labelledby="explanation-heading">
    <h2 id="explanation-heading" style="font-size: var(--text-2xl); color: #0D2137; margin-bottom: 1rem;">
      What Is Medicare Extra Help &amp; How Does It Work?
    </h2>
    <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #0D2137; line-height: 1.6;">
      <strong>Medicare Extra Help</strong> (also called the Low Income Subsidy or LIS) is a federal program authorized by the Medicare Modernization Act and expanded under the Inflation Reduction Act to protect low and moderate-income seniors from high prescription drug costs.
    </p>
    <p style="font-size: 1rem; color: #0D2137; line-height: 1.6;">
      Under 2026 rules, Extra Help provides full assistance to Medicare beneficiaries earning up to 150% of the Federal Poverty Level. The program pays the monthly premium for basic Part D plans, waives annual plan deductibles, eliminates Part D late enrollment penalties, and caps your prescription copayments at designated federal ceilings ($4.90 generic / $12.15 brand).
    </p>
  </section>

  <!-- ═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════
